{"id":"3276aec72d73a2ec3b1ee902711f4c9753f23e4f","axis":"silent","repo":"openvinotoolkit/openvino","sha":"3276aec72d73a2ec3b1ee902711f4c9753f23e4f","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"src/frontends/gguf/docs/quantization.md","lines":["@@ -11,6 +11,21 @@ The implementation is in [`gguf.cpp`](../src/quant/gguf.cpp),"," "," ## Storage and graph conventions"," ","+The loader retains one raw descriptor per original tensor, including its logical shape,","+GGUF format and mapped payload. Builders emit frontend-only `GGUFConstant` leaves and ordinary","+`Concat`, `Slice` and `Gather` operations; they do not unpack or concatenate packed components.","+Normalization folds compatible weight-only row concatenations, slices and gathers before","+repacking directly into the final code, scale and zero-point buffers. It also combines","+compatible two-bit projections sharing an activation. No `GGUFConstant` survives conversion.","+","+Compatible matrix row patterns use the existing native unpacker for each format; plain","+row patterns also fold.","+Inputs must share their format and conversion policy. Aligned column permutations move complete","+quantization groups and may use packed intermediate buffers. Unsupported views, including","+unaligned column gathers, retain ordinary graph operations after leaf materialization.","+Supplied-decoder weights materialize individually using their existing conversion policy.","+Embedding/output policies, quantization groups and zero points are preserved.","+"," The tables below describe the **native `.gguf` input path before device compilation**. The"," [supplied-decoder path](#supplied-decoder-and-raw-byte-differences) has additional conversions."," Mixed checkpoint labels such as `Q4_K_M` select different formats for different tensors; they","@@ -358,9 +373,10 @@ For `N` weights of a uniform block format, multiply its OpenVINO bytes per block"," `N / weights_per_block`. Sum over tensor formats for a mixed checkpoint. This estimates"," frontend payload storage, including per-group metadata."," ","-Native quantized loading allocates independent buffers while reading the memory-mapped","-source. Source pages and output buffers can coexist during import; the loader requests","-eviction of processed source ranges, but this is not a guarantee about peak resident memory.","+Native quantized weights allocate independent buffers when normalization materializes their","+memory-mapped source (or when a caller explicitly invokes the unpacking helper). Source pages and output buffers can coexist","+during import; the loader requests eviction of processed source ranges, but this is not a","+guarantee about peak resident memory."," Splitting or reordering projections can also require copies. Constants built from the"," extracted buffers share those buffers rather than copying each one again."," "],"additions":19,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/frontends/gguf/src/builder/api/graph_context_impl.hpp","lines":["@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ namespace ov::frontend::gguf {"," struct GgufGraphContext::Impl {","     explicit Impl(const BuildContext& ctx)","         : build_ctx(ctx),","-          emitter(ctx.weights->weights, ctx.weights->qtypes, ctx.arch, ctx.weights->translators) {}","+          emitter(ctx.weights->weights, ctx.arch, ctx.weights->translators) {}"," ","     BuildContext build_ctx;","     std::unique_ptr<DecoderConfig> decoder;"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/frontends/gguf/src/builder/api/metadata_store.hpp","lines":["@@ -31,10 +31,9 @@ struct MetadataAccess {","     }"," };"," ","-// Borrowed parser weight and quantization tables.","+// Borrowed parser weight table."," struct WeightStore {","-    std::unordered_map<std::string, ov::Tensor>& weights;","-    std::unordered_map<std::string, GgufTensorType>& qtypes;","+    const GgufWeightTable& weights;","     const std::unordered_map<std::string, CreatorFunction>* translators = nullptr;"," };"," "],"additions":2,"deletions":3,"trunca